# ---- C1_S09: The Letter

== C1_S09.enter
~ set C1_READ_LETTER true

== C1_S09.pages
letter: My {KID},
letter: If you're reading this, then I'm gone, and I think you know where. I'm so sorry I'm not there to make you coffee and pretend I'm not watching you drink it.
letter: I first wrote this the week after Dad's funeral, when you stopped talking to God, and for a while, to me. I've rewritten it every couple of years. This version is from April, the week you moved home. You were so embarrassed. I was so happy. I'm sorry. I was.
letter: Whatever the last thing was that we said to each other, if it was kind, I'm glad. If it was short, don't you dare carry it. I heard the love under it. I always do.
letter: Here's what I believe just happened. I'm not guessing. It's written down, and He keeps His word:
letter: "For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first: Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord." (1 Thessalonians 4:16-17)
letter: In a moment. In the twinkling of an eye (1 Corinthians 15:52). That's how fast. I hope it didn't scare you too badly. I hope I didn't drop anything heavy on your foot.
letter: That means Dad's there too. I'm with your father, {KID}. Isn't that something.
letter: Now the hard part. I won't lie to you, I never have. What comes next will be the hardest time the world has ever seen. Jesus said so Himself (Matthew 24:21). People will be scared and hungry, and they'll do scary, hungry things. Some of them will be our neighbours. Be kind anyway. Be careful anyway.
letter: A man will come with a plan for peace. Everybody will love him. Don't. When they say peace, it isn't:
letter: "For when they shall say, Peace and safety; then sudden destruction cometh upon them." (1 Thessalonians 5:3)
letter: And one day they'll ask you to take a mark, in your hand or on your forehead, so you can buy groceries (Revelation 13:16-17). Whatever they call it, however sweetly they ask, however hungry you are: DON'T. I'm begging you. Read Revelation 14:9-10 if you don't believe me. Then read it again.
letter: But listen. LISTEN. This is the part I've rewritten the most.
letter: It is not too late for you. Not even now. Not even after everything you've said about Him, which, I'll remind you, He heard, and He still wants you.
letter: "That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved." (Romans 10:9)
letter: "For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved." (Romans 10:13)
letter: Whosoever. That's you. I checked.
letter: You don't need the right words. Talk to Him like you talk to me when you're mad. He can take it. He's been knocking on your door for eleven years:
letter: "Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me." (Revelation 3:20)
letter: Practical things, because I'm still your mother:
letter: - The basement. The key is in the sugar tin. Under the stairs: water (12 jugs), cans, the first aid kit, batteries, Dad's camping stove, the hand-crank radio. I know. I KNOW. You laughed at me. Laugh now, I dare you.
letter: - The coffee can on the top shelf has cash. Spend it fast. I don't think cash will last long.
letter: - Dad's toolbox is in the garage. You were always good with your hands. Like him.
letter: - Read my Bible. Start with John. Then read Revelation slowly, with a pencil, and don't skip the scary parts. I underlined what helped me. Maybe it'll help you.
letter: - Ezra Kamau from church may come by. If he's still here, it means he missed it too. Let him in. He's a good man, and he'll be very sad.
letter: I'm not lost, {KID}. I'm home. Jesus promised:
letter: "In my Father's house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you. And if I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again, and receive you unto myself; that where I am, there ye may be also." (John 14:2-3)
letter: There's a place for you too. I asked. I'll be waiting right by the door, and I'll leave the light on.
letter: Come home, {KID}.
letter: All my love, forever and then some,\nMom
~ wait 1.5
letter: P.S. The smoke alarm in the hall needs a 9-volt. I know you forgot.

== C1_S09.after_letter
~ wait 3.0
hero: ...
{C1_HAS_BATTERY == true} hero: I didn't forget.
{C1_HAS_BATTERY == false} hero: I had it. I had it, Mom.
~ wait 1.5
{C1_LAST_WORDS == kind} hero: I said I loved you. At least I said it.
~ wait 1.5
{C1_LAST_WORDS == curt} hero: 'Back in twenty.' That's what I said. Back in twenty.
~ wait 1.5
{C1_LAST_WORDS == joke} hero: You laughed. At least you were laughing.
~ wait 2.0
hero: ...
prompt: Mom's Bible and letter added to your inventory. You can reread them at any time.

== C1_S09.tasks_after
caption: Find the basement key (the sugar tin).

== C1_OBJ_SUGAR_TIN
examine[Sugar tin]: Sugar. And a small brass key wrapped in a sticky note: 'Told you.'

# ---- C1_S10: The Basement

== C1_S10.lines
hero: No. No, no, no.
~ wait 1.5
hero: ...The porch light.
prompt: Find a light. Kitchen drawers.

== C1_S10.tasks
caption: Find a flashlight.
caption: Search the basement.

== C1_OBJ_JUNK_DRAWER
examine[Junk drawer]: Takeout menus, birthday candles, a screwdriver, eleven pens (two work), and a flashlight. Mom labelled it 'FLASHLIGHT.'

== C1_OBJ_STASH_WATER
examine[Water jugs]: Twelve gallon jugs, each dated in marker. The oldest says 2021. She's been rotating them for nine years.

== C1_OBJ_STASH_CANS
examine[Shelves of cans]: Soup, beans, peaches, tuna. Alphabetised. Of course they're alphabetised.

== C1_OBJ_STASH_MEDKIT
examine[First aid kit]: A real one, not a box of bandages. A note taped inside the lid: 'Ask June at the clinic if you don't know what something does.' You don't know a June.

== C1_OBJ_STASH_RADIO
examine[Hand-crank radio]: Still in the box. Dad bought it in 2012, after the big storm. It has a little solar panel.

== C1_OBJ_STASH_STOVE
examine[Dad's camping stove]: Dented green steel. It smells like every camping trip. Two fuel canisters beside it.

== C1_OBJ_STASH_BATTERIES
examine[Box of batteries]: AA, AAA, D. And at the bottom, in its own bag with a sticky note: one 9-volt. 'For when you forget.'

== C1_OBJ_COFFEE_CAN
examine[Coffee can (top shelf)]: Rolled bills, $640, and a folded index card: 'Spend it FAST.'

== C1_OBJ_DAD_WORKBENCH
examine[Dad's old workbench]: His pencil marks are still on the wood. 'Measure twice.' He wrote it there so he'd stop forgetting.

== C1_OBJ_CHRISTMAS_BOX
examine[Box marked 'CHRISTMAS']: Ornaments. On top, the clay angel you made in first grade. It has one wing. Mom put it on top of the tree every single year.

== C1_S10.lines_after_battery
{picked up ITEM_BATTERY_9V from stash} hero: 'For when you forget.'
~ wait 1.0
hero: ...You knew me so well.

